d her growing independence from Gendo.<ref>{{cite web|last=Morton|first=Bryan|access-date=October 20, 2021|url=http://www.fandompost.com/2011/08/12/evangelion-2-22-you-can-not-advance-uk-anime-blu-ray-review/|title=''Evangelion 2.22: You Can (Not) Advance'' UK Anime Blu-ray Review|date=August 12, 2011|website=The Fandom Post|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120323162742/http://www.fandompost.com/2011/08/12/evangelion-2-22-you-can-not-advance-uk-anime-blu-ray-review/|archive-date=March 23, 2012|url-status=live}}</ref> Reviewing the second film, Mark Sombillo of ''Anime News Network'' emphasized her central role in the narrative: "Her personality and plight form much more of the core motivation of the story and despite her still tryingly hesitant attempts at communication, there's genuine warmth beneath her actions and it's hard not to be won over by her."<ref>{{cite web|last=Sombillo|first=Mark|access-date=October 20, 2021|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/evangelion-2.22-you-can-not-advance|title=''Evangelion: 2.22 – You Can (Not) Advance''|date=June 7, 2011|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-date=March 15, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180315201424/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/evangelion-2.22-you-can-not-advance}}</ref> Her role in the final ''Rebuild'' film, ''Evangelion: 3.0+1.0 Thrice Upon a Time'', drew particularly positive reviews for its optimistic outlook<ref>Sources for positive reception to ''Evangelion 3.0+1.0'':
